WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.720
Speaker 1: Florida is at the center of a&nbsp;
Republican civil war that I absolutely love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:12.240
Florida Republican Governor Ron DeSantis is almost&nbsp;
certainly going to win reelection. It's just what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.260
the polls say and everybody should get out there&nbsp;
and vote for Charlie Crist. But in all likelihood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.300
the winner is going to be Ron DeSantis. Donald&nbsp;
Trump has announced a series of rallies, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.540
in Florida, in support of 2022 candidates. He is&nbsp;
doing a rally in Florida with Marco Rubio, who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:34.740
running for reelection to the Senate. But Ron&nbsp;
DeSantis is conspicuously excluded from that. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:42.000
know what this is all about, my friends. This is&nbsp;
a snub because Trump is furious with the Santos.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.540
DeSantis, when asked, has not ruled out running in&nbsp;
2024 for the Republican presidential nomination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:58.080
even if even if Donald Trump wants the nomination&nbsp;
as well. Donald Trump expects unending loyalty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:05.640
from other Republicans. What Trump wants the&nbsp;
Santos to have said is, I won't challenge Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.400
Trump. This nomination is Trump's if he wants it.&nbsp;
If he doesn't, then I'll think about my political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.680
future. DeSantis hasn't done that. And why hasn't&nbsp;
DeSantis done it? Well, if you look at the betting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:22.740
markets, you see that DeSantis is essentially&nbsp;
running tied with Donald Trump. When you ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:28.080
people, who do you believe will be the Republican&nbsp;
nominee? These aren't polls in the polls. Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.540
is still doing much better. These are betting&nbsp;
markets. DeSantis and Trump have been right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:39.540
neck and neck for a couple of months at this&nbsp;
point in time. DeSantis knows he is positioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:44.940
to maybe be the Republican presidential nominee,&nbsp;
which would be a big boon for him, without a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:52.020
doubt. And this is making Trump furious. Politico&nbsp;
reports Trump to hold rally in Florida with Rubio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:59.280
but not DeSantis. The apparent snub are angered&nbsp;
some people within DeSantis orbit who complained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.160
that the Florida governor's team was not informed&nbsp;
of the rally prior. It is abundantly clear what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:11.820
is going on here. Donald Trump correctly and&nbsp;
accurately sees Ron DeSantis as a threat to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:18.720
Trump's potential. Desire to be the Republican&nbsp;
nominee in 2024. And so this civil war is growing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:24.000
and growing and growing. I've told you before the&nbsp;
numerous reports of Donald Trump privately fuming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.920
at Ron DeSantis, and increasingly we have seen&nbsp;
Ron DeSantis publicly distance himself from Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.920
Trump when it comes to Florida's COVID response&nbsp;
and other things. This is a great thing. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:42.840
a great thing. The more strife there is from now,&nbsp;
because lesson 2024 starts in 12 days after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.780
November midterm, the more strife there is between&nbsp;
these folks. Leading up to the primary, I believe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:55.080
the more they will weaken each other and hopefully&nbsp;
hurt themselves in the eventual general election&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:00.780
of 2024. We will have plenty of time to&nbsp;
discuss that, but you really love to see it.

